## F3. What to tell the team

- **It is an extension.** AGENTS.md keeps the team's active comparison frozen. This work adds
  two policies next to it and changes no workload, simulator setting or existing result.
  Putting it into the final report needs the team's agreement.
- **It is small.** The rule is about 30 lines in `RUSHI_Task/same_job/policy.py`, built on
  Rohan's class. With the rule switched off, it is Rohan's policy exactly.
- **On novelty:** say "to our knowledge" and cite LAVA and the MinUsageTime work. Run a proper
  Google Scholar check before calling it a first.
- **Possible next steps:** repair the memory-aware score itself (Part B2), so the *first*
  task of each job also goes to a busy server; and check the rule on task samples nobody has
  looked at.
